#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:414
msgid ""
"Lowers to the CUDA helper `tl::get_lane_idx(warp_size)` defined in `src/"
"tl_templates/cuda/intrin.h`, which computes the lane index from the linear "
"thread id using the provided `warp_size`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:423
#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:441
msgid "Logical warp size used for the index calculation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:433
msgid ""
"Emits `tl::get_warp_idx_sync(warp_size)` which divides the block-linear "
"thread id by `warp_size`, matching the semantics of CUTLASS' canonical "
"helpers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:451
msgid ""
"Lowers to `tl::get_warp_idx(warp_size)` which divides the block-linear "
"thread id by the provided `warp_size` without requiring warp convergence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:459
msgid "Logical warp size to use (defaults to 32 on NVIDIA / 64 on AMD)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:461
msgid "Number of warps per warp-group. Defaults to 4 on NVIDIA architectures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:471
msgid ""
"Generates `tl::get_warp_group_idx(warp_size, warps_per_group)` which divides "
"the block-linear thread id by `warp_size * warps_per_group`, matching the "
"canonical ordering while allowing architecture-specific overrides."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:480
msgid ""
"Size (in threads) of the group in which a single lane should be elected. "
"Passing 0 elects a single lane in the entire thread block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:491
msgid ""
"Lowered to the CUDA helper `tl::tl_shuffle_elect<thread_extent>()` defined "
"in `src/tl_templates/cuda/intrin.h`, which relies on `cutlass::"
"canonical_warp_idx()` and `cute::elect_one_sync()` to pick one lane per "
"group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:501
msgid ""
"This prevents NVCC from sinking uses of accumulator fragments past the "
"corresponding WGMMA operations by issuing an empty inline assembly barrier "
"on every register."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:504
msgid ""
"BufferLikeType | PrimExpr A buffer representing the accumulator fragment, a "
"buffer load/region that identifies a starting element within the fragment, "
"or a pointer expression (e.g., tvm_access_ptr/address_of/typed Var)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:508
msgid ""
"int | PrimExpr Element offset from the start of the accumulator fragment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:510
msgid ""
"int | PrimExpr | None Number of 32-bit registers to fence. If None and a "
"Buffer is provided, it will be derived from the buffer shape and dtype."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:513
msgid ""
"DType | None Data type string of the accumulator elements. When passing a "
"buffer or buffer-derived expression, dtype is inferred. It is required only "
"when passing a raw pointer expression that cannot be inferred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:518
msgid "A handle to the warpgroup fence operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:526
msgid "int The id of the WGMMA operation to wait for"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:529
msgid "A handle to the WGMMA wait operation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:537
msgid "BarrierType The memory barrier to wait on"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:539
msgid "int | Var The parity value to wait for"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:545
msgid ""
"Current implementation is a sugar syntax for mbarrier_wait_parity, as we "
"only support parity 0 and 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:558
msgid ""
"XOR-swap ``value`` across lanes (``__shfl_xor_sync`` on CUDA, ``__shfl_xor`` "
"on HIP — mask ignored on HIP)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:564
msgid ""
"Shift ``value`` down by ``delta`` lanes (``__shfl_down_sync`` on CUDA, "
"``__shfl_down`` on HIP)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:570
msgid ""
"Shift ``value`` up by ``delta`` lanes (``__shfl_up_sync`` on CUDA, "
"``__shfl_up`` on HIP)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:583
msgid ""
"Signals that the calling threads have arrived at the named barrier without "
"waiting for other participants.  Unlike ``T.sync_threads(barrier_id, n)`` "
"which maps to ``bar.sync`` (arrive + wait), this call only *arrives* and "
"returns immediately, allowing the calling warp group to continue working "
"while the other side waits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:589
msgid "This is useful in warp-specialized producer/consumer pipelines:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:591
msgid ""
"# Producer warp group: signal readiness, keep going\n"
"T.named_barrier_arrive(ready_barrier, total_threads)\n"
"\n"
"# Consumer warp group: block until producer has arrived\n"
"T.sync_threads(ready_barrier, total_threads)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:599
msgid "Named barrier index (0-15). May be a variable (PrimExpr)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:600
msgid ""
"Total number of CTA threads participating in the barrier. May be a variable "
"(PrimExpr)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:603
msgid ""
"Lowers to: ``asm volatile(\"bar.arrive %0, %1;\" : : \"r\"(id), \"r\"(cnt));"
"``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:613
msgid ""
"Broadcast ``value`` from ``srcLane`` to all lanes in the subgroup of "
"``width`` lanes (``__shfl_sync`` on CUDA, ``__shfl`` on HIP — mask ignored "
"on HIP)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:622
msgid ""
"Lowers to ``__any_sync(mask, predicate)`` on CUDA and ``__any(predicate)`` "
"on HIP (the mask is ignored on HIP because the full wavefront is always "
"convergent)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:626
#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:640
msgid "Integer condition to test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/builtin/index.rst:627
